# rec2iter is an LCCC transformation: the pass rewrites the exponential
# double recursion into an O(n) iteration, which is the whole point of the
# test (fib(90) is instant for LCCC and billions of years for GCC).  The
# reference compiler has no such pass, so its leg is not a slow oracle but a
# non-terminating one -- the runner kills it at the per-test timeout and the
# comparison can only ever fail.  LCCC's own result is still checked: the
# program returns non-zero unless every fib() matches the expected value, and
# the run:ok phase requires that exit status.
LCCC_NO_COMPARE=1
